# NYBOSS .NET Project Creation

## Phase 1

The current implementation creates the project structure only.

The generator must not create application-level classes or business logic.

## Default Business Project

When no specific project structure is provided, create:

<ProjectName>/
├── <ProjectName>.API/
├── <ProjectName>.Common/
├── <ProjectName>.Repository/
└── <ProjectName>.Services/

Example:

Customer/
├── Customer.API/
├── Customer.Common/
├── Customer.Repository/
└── Customer.Services/

## Project Types

### API

Use the ASP.NET Core Web API project template.

Conceptually:

dotnet new webapi

The generated project must use the new project name:

<ProjectName>.API

### Common

Use a .NET class library.

Conceptually:

dotnet new classlib

Project name:

<ProjectName>.Common

### Repository

Use a .NET class library.

Conceptually:

dotnet new classlib

Project name:

<ProjectName>.Repository

### Services

Use a .NET class library.

Conceptually:

dotnet new classlib

Project name:

<ProjectName>.Services

## Project Creation Order

For the default project, create projects in this order:

1. Common
2. Repository
3. Services
4. API

This allows project references to be established after all required projects exist.

## Basic Internal References

For the default project, use only references between the newly created projects.

Expected basic dependency direction:

API
→ Services

Services
→ Common
→ Repository

Repository
→ Common

Common
→ no generated project dependency

Do not add external NYBOSS repository references during default project creation.

## Solution Registration

The projects must be added to:

BNPP.NYBOSS.NextGen.Server.sln

Example:

dotnet sln BNPP.NYBOSS.NextGen.Server.sln add Apps/Business/Customer/Customer.Common/Customer.Common.csproj

Repeat for each generated project.

## Explicit Components

If the user specifies components, create only the requested components.

Example:

Create Customer with Common and Services

Result:

Customer/
├── Customer.Common/
└── Customer.Services/

Do not automatically add API, Repository, MessageProcessing, or Host.

## Existing Project Pattern

If the user specifies:

"similar to ManualForecast"

inspect:

Apps/Business/ManualForecast/

Determine its project composition.

For example, if the reference contains:

ManualForecast.API
ManualForecast.Common
ManualForecast.MessageProcessing
ManualForecast.MessageProcessingHost
ManualForecast.Repository
ManualForecast.Services

then the new project should contain equivalent components:

Customer.API
Customer.Common
Customer.MessageProcessing
Customer.MessageProcessingHost
Customer.Repository
Customer.Services

Only the structure is reused.

The existing project naming convention is not reused.

## Existing Project Pattern Example

If the user says:

"Create TradeSettlement similar to TradeLifeStatus"

inspect the actual TradeLifeStatus directory before creating the new project.

If its composition is:

Aft.Services
Odin.Services
TradeLifeStatus.Common
TradeLifeStatus.Repository
TradeLifeStatusInternal.Host
TradeLifeStatusInternal.Services

the new project names should follow the new convention and the requested project name.

Do not add the legacy BNPP.NYBOSS prefix.

## Project Contents

Do not create application contents during Phase 1.

For example, do not automatically create:

Controllers/
Models/
Services/
Repositories/
Interfaces/
Handlers/

unless they are required as part of the project template itself or explicitly requested.

The objective of Phase 1 is project creation, not feature implementation.
